shithub is the command-line client for shithub.sh — a feature-complete,
AGPLv3-licensed reverse engineering of GitHub. The command tree mirrors
GitHub's gh CLI; flags and output shapes are gh-compatible where shithub's
data model permits.

Authentication, configuration, and host management live under
'shithub auth' and 'shithub config'. The 'shithub api' escape hatch
exposes the raw REST surface for anything the typed subcommands have not
yet wrapped.

Usage:
  shithub [command]

Available Commands:
  alias       Create command shortcuts
  api         Make an authenticated HTTP request to a shithub API endpoint
  attestation Verify and inspect Sigstore artifact attestations (deferred until Sigstore integration ships)
  auth        Authenticate shithub-cli and configure git credential helpers
  browse      Open the shithub repository in a browser
  cache       Manage GitHub-Actions-compatible cache entries
  completion  Print a shell completion script
  config      Read and write shithub-cli configuration
  extension   Install and manage third-party shithub-cli extensions
  gist        Manage gists (deferred until shithub-S49 ships)
  gpg-key     Manage your shithub GPG public keys
  help        Help about any command
  issue       Manage issues
  label       Manage repository labels
  org         Work with organizations
  pr          Manage pull requests
  project     Manage ProjectsV2-style projects (deferred until shithub-S47 ships)
  release     Manage releases (deferred until shithub-S48 ships)
  repo        Manage repositories
  ruleset     Inspect repository and org rulesets (deferred until REST API ships)
  run         Inspect workflow runs and their artifacts
  search      Search across repos, issues, PRs, code, and commits
  secret      Manage GitHub-Actions-style secrets
  ssh-key     Manage your shithub SSH public keys
  status      Personal dashboard: assigned issues, PRs, review requests, mentions
  variable    Manage GitHub-Actions-style variables
  version     Print version information
  workflow    Inspect and trigger GitHub-Actions-style workflows

Flags:
  -h, --help      help for shithub
  -v, --version   version for shithub

Use "shithub [command] --help" for more information about a command.
